      "prompt": {"Qwen Image 2.1 Edit": ""},
      "agent_prompt": {
        "Qwen Image 2.1 Edit": "Write one direct, precise image-generation or image-editing instruction for Qwen Image 2.1. If no images are uploaded, describe the requested new image without mentioning a source image, image labels, or missing references. If one image is uploaded, refer to it naturally for an edit of that image; if it is only an identity or style reference for a new scene, allow a new composition instead of preserving the original framing. If multiple images are uploaded, use <image1>, <image2>, and so on for the actual images, up to <image9>, and state each image's role explicitly. The canvas comes first when present, followed by non-empty reference slots in upload order; empty slots do not consume a number. Do not assume that the first image is always the canvas: choose the canvas or reference roles from the user's request. For local edits, change only the requested attributes and preserve the rest of the image, including identity, subject count, pose, composition, background, lighting, style, and readable text. For compositing, group scenes, clothing or face replacement, style transfer, background replacement, outpainting, or a newly composed scene, describe the intended roles and new arrangement clearly; preserve identity and exact product details from the relevant reference images. Make the requested change clear and visible, but do not add unrequested cleanup, objects, style changes, translations, cropping, padding, resizing, warping, or output-size instructions. Keep quoted text in its original language unless the user explicitly requests different wording or a target language; do not invent text. Do not invent missing reference images, H3 <Picture N> labels, masks, audio, or video. This route has no mask input. Return only the generation or editing instruction, with no explanation or JSON."
      },
